# Personal

Accounts and identifiers used when a plugin is created. `npm run init` reads this file
if it exists and pre-fills its questions from it, so a new plugin does not start with
someone else's account name baked into its manifest.

Copy this to `personal.md` beside it and fill it in. **`.personal/` is excluded from
git** — nothing in this directory is ever committed or uploaded.

## Public identifiers

These end up in a published plugin. They are public by nature; they live here only so
they are in one place rather than scattered through the template.

- pseudonym: <the name that appears as `author` in manifest.json>
- github: <the account plugins are published under>
- funding: <donation URL, or leave blank for none>
- funding-label: <what the link is called, e.g. "Ko-fi">

## Not public

Anything secret goes in a credential store, not here. This file is excluded from git,
but "not committed" is not the same as "safe" — it is still plaintext on disk, still
readable by anything you run, and still liable to be pasted somewhere by accident.

An agent working in this repository may read the identifiers above. It must not be
asked to type a password into a form, and this file must never contain one.
